      ],
      "source": "https://townofhighland.wi.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Brule River in Highland was once a vital route for explorers traveling from Lake Superior to the Mississippi River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhighland.wi.gov/our-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sueur Danial Graysolon Dulhut, the namesake for the city of Duluth, was the first European of record to traverse the Brule in 1680.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhighland.wi.gov/our-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Highland was originally inhabited by the Sioux and Chippewa Indians, who fought for many years over the local territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhighland.wi.gov/our-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cedar Island in Highland features an estate established in the 1880s by Henry Clay Pierce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://townofhighland.wi.gov/our-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Great pine forests once covered most of the Highland township before the arrival of lumbermen in 1897.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
